GUARDIANA for Windows\par
\par
Guardiana shows you which services your AI talks to and, with Home Mode, every device on your Wi-Fi: it explains each one in a sentence and cuts only what you decide. Everything happens on this PC. No account, no server of ours, zero telemetry.\par
\par
What this installer will do\par
- Copy the program to "Program Files\\Guardiana".\par
- Register the "Guardiana" service, which starts with Windows.\par
- Add the "Guardiana" shortcut to the Start menu, which opens the panel in your browser.\par
- Make Guardiana this PC's DNS, over IPv6 too, so it starts watching from the first minute. It first keeps an exact copy of your setting; if the service stops, the PC gets its previous DNS back, and uninstalling leaves it exactly as it was.\par
\par
What it will NOT do\par
- It does not read what you send or receive: only the service name, the time and the device.\par
- It opens no port to the network. Only Home Mode, when you turn it on, listens on your home Wi-Fi; turning it off closes it.\par
\par
After installing\par
The panel opens when the installer finishes and within a minute you will see this PC's queries. To put the DNS back as it was without uninstalling: panel, "Status". Cutting one specific name works from the first minute; wide cuts, by category or for the whole home, wait until Guardiana has been watching that device for 24 hours.\par
\par
Seven days with everything and no card; after that you need a subscription. What was written down stays on your disk, whether you pay or not.\par
\par
